<title>SINGAPORE: IPC slumps to 1996 net loss.</title>
<headline>IPC slumps to 1996 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 23.90 vs  52.67 (profit)</p>
<p>    Net loss *			     23.90 vs  52.67 (profit)</p>
<p>    Final dividend (percent)	   10.00 vs  16.00</p>
<p>    Post-tax op. profit/shr (cents)   1.35 vs   5.27</p>
<p>    Turnover				801.90 vs 1,542.35</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 3.29 vs   2.02</p>
<p>    Interest expense			7.87 vs  10.43</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	   6.22 vs  13.65</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 13.74 vs  54.30</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		  2.00 vs   1.22 (profit)</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.28 vs   0.80</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (profit) 2.06 vs   2.04 (loss)</p>
<p>    Post-tax op. profit		  13.53 vs  52.67</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss		   37.43 vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - IPC Corp Ltd makes computers.</p>
<p>* 1996 figure includes extraordinary loss.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
